From ec4dbd88f695a5caa6cd04e39d9bb07057ba943e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Duprey <509630+destinal@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 13:01:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 03/17] Add OSC 21337 tab status

iTerm2 3.7 lets programs report a session's status with OSC 21337, and
its Claude Code integration uses this to show whether a session is
working, waiting or idle:

  printf '\e]21337;status=Working;indicator=#ffa500\a'

Konsole now parses the sequence into a TabStatusUpdate and emits
Session::tabStatusReceived. Parsing follows iTerm2: semicolon-separated
key=value pairs with \; and \\ escapes; status, indicator, status-color
and detail fields, where an empty value clears the field; colors as
#RRGGBB or xterm rgb:R/G/B. With expires-on=progress-end the status lasts
until the program's OSC 9;4 progress ends, replaced by the then-* fields
or cleared if there are none.

Konsole does not display the status itself; the signal is for plugins.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
